# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend switches environment through `.env` (one line, ENVIRONMENT=name)
# and reads its settings from `.env.<name>` beside it.
#
# `backend/.env` and `backend/.env.local` are committed, because neither holds
# anything secret — the local credentials address containers on a private
# compose network and are useless outside it. Committing them is what lets a
# fresh clone run with no copying step.
#
# Everything else matching `.env.*` is a real deployment's credentials: ignored
# deny-by-default, so `backend/.env.production` — or a `.env.staging` nobody
# anticipated — cannot be committed by accident.
#
# The exception is scoped to `backend/` on purpose. `frontend/.env.local` is a
# Next.js file, where the convention is the opposite: it is where local secrets
# go and it must stay ignored. An unscoped `!.env.local` would expose it.
.env.*
!backend/.env.local
.data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend test suite is tracked on purpose. The base template ignored
# `tests/*`, which would have excluded the seat lock concurrency tests; only
# the caches below are ignored.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Backend runtime scratch directory
backend/app/temp/

